    "updated_at": "2026-11-25T18:17:59Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/4041-ui-link-owner-flake · PR #4048 · pinned by ui_link_owner::a_false_server_that_proves_the_token_gets_no_tool_call_when_the_window_has_ended and ui_link_owner::a_crashed_windows_file_is_removed_and_its_port_is_never_dialed (200 of 200 looped runs of mcp_live) · merges when reviewed\n\nCause: on Unix a flock belongs to the open file. A child that another thread starts holds a copy of each descriptor until its exec, so a close does not release the lock in that time. link_owner::owner (product code of PR #4020) and the tests released the lock only by a close. Now they unlock first.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
